      "output": {
        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "Obligations from `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.ask`:\n1. `ask::<R>()` starts an agent request whose submitted answer is decoded as `R`.\n2. The request's graph tools record reads in the same dependency list as direct reads (`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.shared_context`, cited).\n3. The signature (`R: DeserializeOwned + JsonSchema + Send`, `Ask<'_, 'd, D, R, ContextPhase>`).\n\nCoverage:\n- Decoding as `R`: `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` calls `ctx.ask::<Answer>()` and asserts `answer.n == 7`. It also asserts the JSON schema sent to the agent has `properties.n.type == \"integer\"`. It also calls `assert_send` on the future. `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[verify_returns_direct_and_tool_reads_in_one_trace]` asks for `bool`, and the submitted `{\"result\": true}` is decoded.\n- Shared dependency list: `verify_returns_direct_and_tool_reads_in_one_trace` has the criterion read node 42 directly. It then calls `cx.ask::<bool>()`, and the agent's `read_node` tool reads node 7. The test asserts the returned dependencies contain both nodes, in order, in a single list. It also asserts the server saw 2 requests. `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace` shows that direct reads before and after an `ask` and the ask's own reads all end up in `ctx.dependencies()`. A later `ask` leaves that list unchanged.\n- Signature and bounds: `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` compiles the Habeas consumer against the SDK and checks the exports. The explicit-insertions test also exercises the `Send` bound.\n\nThe cited `shared_context` rule that a subsequent verification starts empty is not part of this requirement's own obligations, and the other tests cover its main shared-trace behavior. I found no gap."
      }
